    "description": {
      "content": "sandbox-svc — the favorite-items feature (FEAT-001).\n\nThree routes: favorite an item, list your favorites, un-favorite one. Every\nroute acts on the calling user's own rows only; the user is taken from the\naccess token, never from the request, so no route accepts a user id.\n\nThis document is hand-maintained. nexcommon's swagger generator\n(`NewHandleFuncParam`) resets a path's method map on every registration, so\nit emits only the last route registered on a shared path and drops\n`POST /v1/favorites`. The service itself routes and tags all three\ncorrectly — the generated document is the only thing that loses one. See\n`docs/FEAT-001/dev-test-results.md`'s Known limitations.\n",
